```apex
public class AccountCountrySync {

    public static void handle() {
        // 1. Identify accounts whose BillingCountry actually changed.
        Map<Id, Account> oldMap = new Map<Id, Account>(Trigger.old);
        Set<Id> changedAccountIds = new Set<Id>();

        for (Account acc : Trigger.new) {
            Account oldAcc = oldMap.get(acc.Id);
            if (oldAcc != null && acc.BillingCountry != oldAcc.BillingCountry) {
                changedAccountIds.add(acc.Id);
            }
        }

        if (changedAccountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // 2. One query: load contacts belonging only to the changed accounts.
        //    Filtered by AccountId so we never hit the 50k-row SOQL cap,
        //    regardless of total contact volume in the org.
        Map<Id, List<Contact>> contactsByAccount = new Map<Id, List<Contact>>();
        for (Contact c : [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :changedAccountIds
        ]) {
            if (!contactsByAccount.containsKey(c.AccountId)) {
                contactsByAccount.put(c.AccountId, new List<Contact>());
            }
            contactsByAccount.get(c.AccountId).add(c);
        }

        // 3. Determine which contacts to update.
        //    A contact qualifies when its MailingCountry is blank OR
        //    still matches the account's *previous* BillingCountry.
        List<Contact> toUpdate = new List<Contact>();

        for (Account acc : Trigger.new) {
            if (!changedAccountIds.contains(acc.Id)) {
                continue;
            }

            String oldCountry = oldMap.get(acc.Id).BillingCountry;
            String newCountry = acc.BillingCountry;
            List<Contact> accContacts = contactsByAccount.get(acc.Id);

            if (accContacts == null) {
                continue;
            }

            for (Contact c : accContacts) {
                if (String.isBlank(c.MailingCountry) || c.MailingCountry == oldCountry) {
                    c.MailingCountry = newCountry;
                    toUpdate.add(c);
                }
            }
        }

        // 4. Persist changes.
        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

### Key design notes

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **50k SOQL row cap** | Query is filtered to `WHERE AccountId IN :changedAccountIds`; with 200-account MDM batches the result set stays small. |
| **No queries in loops** | Exactly one SOQL statement, one DML statement. |
| **Contacts in other countries** | Excluded by the `isBlank / == oldCountry` guard — they keep their own `MailingCountry`. |
| **Accounts with no country change** | Excluded early; no contacts are even fetched for them. |
| **Country set to null** | If `BillingCountry` is cleared, qualifying contacts get `MailingCountry = null` (they "follow" the account). |
| **Re-entrancy / recursion** | Updating Contact does not fire Account triggers, so no loop risk. |
| **Rollback safety** | Because this is an after-trigger with DML, a failure in the `update` will roll back the entire transaction (including the account changes), keeping data consistent. |

