**Key design decisions:**

- **Unique ID generation:** A module-scoped counter (`uid`) is incremented in each instance's `constructor`, guaranteeing a unique `id` per rendered instance even when multiple `<c-collapsible-section>` elements appear on the same page. Because LWC shares the module across instances but each instance runs its own constructor, the counter is both safe and simple.

- **`hidden` attribute as a presence attribute:** The getter `bodyHidden` returns a boolean. LWC's attribute binding treats `true` as "add the attribute" and `false` as "remove the attribute," so the `hidden` attribute appears/disappears exactly as the WAI-ARIA disclosure pattern requires.

- **`aria-controls` always resolves:** The `<div class="section-body">` is never conditionally rendered (`if:`) — it is always in the DOM. Toggling only flips the `hidden` attribute, so the `aria-controls` reference on the button remains valid at all times.

