        <template for:each={results} for:item="contact">
            <li key={contact.Id} data-id={contact.Id}>{contact.Name}</li>
        </template>
    </ul>
</template>
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| Debounce (300 ms) | `clearTimeout` + `setTimeout` in `handleSearch`; the timeout callback reads the latest value stored in `_searchTerm`. |
| Fewer than 2 chars | Inside `_performSearch`, trim and check length; if < 2, clear results and return without calling Apex. |
| Out-of-order responses | Monotonic `_requestId` counter; each Apex call captures the id at call time and the `.then`/`.catch` compare it to the current `_requestId`. Stale responses are silently discarded. |
| Component disconnected while pending | Both the debounce timeout callback (`_performSearch`) and each Apex callback check `this.isConnected` before touching state. If the component has been removed, the search either never fires (debounce case) or its result is discarded (in-flight case). |
| Error display | `error` holds the string from `err.body.message`; the `<p class="error">` is conditionally rendered with `if:true={error}`. |

