```apex
public class AccountOwnershipService {

    /**
     * Reassigns ownership of the specified Accounts and all their Contacts to newOwnerId.
     * 
     * - Account trigger actions are bypassed for the duration of the Account DML
     *   (and any Contact-triggered Account DML) via TAF's sObject-level bypass.
     * - Contact trigger actions run normally.
     * - The bypass is guaranteed to be cleared in a finally block, so Account
     *   automation resumes normal behaviour for the rest of the transaction
     *   regardless of success or failure.
     * - All-or-none: both DML statements share the same transaction; if either
     *   fails the exception propagates and the whole transaction rolls back.
     * - Bulk-safe: exactly 2 SOQL queries and at most 2 DML statements
     *   regardless of input volume (up to 200 accounts).
     */
    public static void reassign(Set<Id> accountIds, Id newOwnerId) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // --- SOQL (2 queries total) ---
        List<Account> accounts = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM Account
            WHERE Id IN :accountIds
        ];
        List<Contact> contacts = [
            SELECT Id, AccountId
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
        ];

        // Mutate in memory
        for (Account acct : accounts) {
            acct.OwnerId = newOwnerId;
        }
        for (Contact c : contacts) {
            c.OwnerId = newOwnerId;
        }

        // --- DML with TAF bypass (at most 2 DML statements) ---
        TriggerBase.bypass('Account');
        try {
            if (!accounts.isEmpty()) {
                update accounts;
            }
            if (!contacts.isEmpty()) {
                update contacts;
            }
        } finally {
            TriggerBase.clearBypass('Account');
        }
    }
}
```

**Design rationale:**

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| No Account trigger actions during ownership change | `TriggerBase.bypass('Account')` suppresses all TAF-registered actions on Account for the current transaction |
| Contact trigger actions run normally | Only Account is bypassed; Contact is untouched, so its TAF actions fire as usual |
| Bypass cleared on success **and** failure | `finally` block guarantees `clearBypass` runs even when an exception is thrown |
| All-or-none DML | Both `update` statements execute in the same transaction; any DML failure rolls back both |
| Exceptions propagate unchanged | No `catch` block—only `try/finally`—so the original exception (or DML validation error) is re-thrown to the caller after the `finally` executes |
| ≤ 2 SOQL, ≤ 2 DML regardless of volume | One query for Accounts, one for Contacts; one `update` per collection (guarded by `isEmpty`) |
| Bulk-safe for 200 accounts | No per-record loops around SOQL or DML; all work is in-memory list mutation followed by two bulk `update` calls |

